Tell apps where the display cut-outs are (needs 0007 and 0008).

Reads Silica's /desktop/sailfish/silica/cutouts from dconf (set by the device
adaptation, e.g. [[310, 0, 414, 66]] = [x, y, width, height] in native panel
pixels). Fullscreen wl_shell windows cover the whole panel, so for those the
cut-outs are mapped into view coordinates for the current rotation and sent
on the JSON message channel flutter-sfos/display_cutouts, together with the
padding that keeps content clear of them (physical pixels):

  {"version": 1,
   "padding": {"top": 66, "right": 0, "bottom": 0, "left": 0},
   "cutouts": [{"left": 310, "top": 0, "width": 414, "height": 66}]}

Sent once the engine is running and again when the orientation or window size
changes; repeats are skipped. xdg_shell windows get no cut-outs, because
Lipstick already keeps them clear.

The embedder API has no view padding, so apps apply it themselves (see
docs/PORTING.md).

